ent. Australia got off to a poor start, placing only sixth in the dressage, which was led by the United States, with Great Britain second, New Zealand third, and Canada and Germany in fourth and fifth, respectively. The US team placed only fifth in the endurance phase, however, which was won by Australia who moved into first place overall, with a 61.00 point lead over the Americans, with New Zealand further back in third. Australia was again only sixth in jumping, but their lead was insurmountable, as the United States placed fourth in the jumping, and Australia defended their gold medal comfortably. The US finished second with New Zealand third. Australia would again win this event at Sydney in 2000, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/12141"} "Andrew Hoy"] " competing on all three gold-medal winning teams from 1992-2000."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "Horse"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Australia"] [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "-203.85"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "134"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/11452"} "Wendy Schaeffer"] " "] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/2387"} "Sunburst"]]] [:td {}] [:td {} "-61.00"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "135"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/11906"} "Phillip Dutton"] " "] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/2517"} "True Blue Girdwood"]]] [:td {}] [:td {} "-69.40"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "131"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12141"} "Andrew Hoy"] " "] [:td {